---
title: 'HLC Series'
enterprise: true
---

An HLC Series shows high, low and close data as a line through the close values, with shaded bands reaching up to the high values and down to the low values.

## Simple HLC

{% chartExampleRunner title="Simple HLC" name="simple-hlc" type="generated" /%}

To create an HLC Series, use the `hlc` series type.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'hlc',
            xKey: 'date',
            highKey: 'high',
            lowKey: 'low',
            closeKey: 'close',
        },
    ],
}
```

In this configuration:

- `xKey` sets the x value.
- `highKey` sets the high values.
- `lowKey` sets the low values.
- `closeKey` sets the close values.

The series is drawn as a band from the close to the high, a band from the low to the close, and a line through the close values. These are all part of the same series, so there is a single legend item, and a single tooltip for each data item.

## Customisation

{% chartExampleRunner title="HLC Customisations" name="hlc-customisations" type="generated" /%}

Series items are customised via the `item` configuration object.

The properties `item.high`, `item.low` and `item.close` control the display of the high band, the low band and the close line respectively.

- `item.high` styles the band from the close to the high, and the high edge.
- `item.low` styles the band from the low to the close, and the low edge.
- `item.close` styles the close line.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'hlc',
            // ...
            item: {
                high: {
                    fillOpacity: 0.2,
                    lineDash: [4, 4],
                },
                low: {
                    fillOpacity: 0.2,
                    lineDash: [4, 4],
                },
                close: {
                    strokeWidth: 3,
                    marker: {
                        enabled: true,
                        shape: 'diamond',
                        size: 8,
                    },
                },
            },
        },
    ],
}
```

## Markers

Markers are not shown by default. Set `marker.enabled` to show markers on the high, low and close values, or enable them for a single value with `item.high.marker`, `item.low.marker` or `item.close.marker`, as in the example above.

Use `marker.itemStyler` to style individual markers. It is called once for each marker, with an `itemType` of `'high'`, `'low'` or `'close'`.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'hlc',
            // ...
            marker: {
                enabled: true,
                itemStyler: ({ itemType }) => {
                    return { size: itemType === 'close' ? 8 : 4 };
                },
            },
        },
    ],
}
```

